    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 22-layer TiO2/SiO2 dichroic coating on fused silica substrate at 45° incidence. Initialize all layer thicknesses from analytic quarter-wave values at λ₀=550 nm (TiO2 d_H≈52 nm, SiO2 d_L≈96 nm) with ±3 nm random perturbation. Apply hard geometric bounds [20,150] nm on all thicknesses. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with step-size multiplier reduced by 40% relative to baseline. Generate 12 candidate solutions. Evaluate target score as weighted combination of mean reflectance (450-650 nm) and mean transmittance (700-1000 nm). Layer sequence: TiO2|SiO2|TiO2|SiO2|TiO2|SiO2|TiO2|SiO2|TiO2|SiO2|TiO2|SiO2|TiO2|SiO2|TiO2|SiO2|TiO2|SiO2|TiO2|SiO2|TiO2|SiO2 (22 finite layers total). Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 450-650 nm, 700-1000 nm. soft objectives: high reflectance in 450-650 nm; high transmittance in 700-1000 nm; minimized crosstalk between bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 450-650 nm; reflectance in 700-1000 nm. manufacturing constraints: maximum 24 layers.",
